  "summary": "Several NAR database updates and an infectious-disease knowledge graph pair expanded content with API, client-library and agentic access.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is curated biomolecular resources growing in content while becoming easier to query by machine. PDBe adds literature-mined residue annotations, MD simulation links via MDposit, MOLE pore analyses, and API plus MCP agentic access. GPCRdb expands structure and ligand coverage, including Boltz-2 and AlphaFold2-Multimer models. DGIdb adds Python and R clients, Docker images and versioned releases. HIPPIE 3.0 grows to about 1.2M experimentally supported PPIs and adds negative training sets; PRGdb 5.0 adds DREM deep-learning prioritization across 874,967 candidate proteins. IDKG, a preprint, integrates 20 sources in a Neo4j graph. Predicted models, learned prioritization and machine-oriented interfaces are the new elements, though not every resource is structure-centered.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
